  "about": "The English messages the Lights move introduced (src/core/i18n/en.ts, lights.*), each with sample values: the model's (#259), the commands' toasts (#261) and the pane's saves (#260). test/unit/i18n/moved-strings.test.ts asserts that the French catalog renders what the rewrite layer makes of the English, or what is `translated` where the layer left the English as it stood: \"No lights found\" on the tablet's card, the pane's three Adaptive Lighting lines and the picker's \"now with\", a visible change that #260 and #262 record in their baselines. A tile's accessible name is read with its line in French, as the layer read the whole label. #263 deleted the map entries the legacy panel no longer renders once the pane (#260) and the sheet (#262) moved: `was` is what the layer made of the English before, `after` what it makes of it now. The entries other screens still render (Lights, Other lights, the light counts of the Home tile, the stack and the room chips) stay. Deleted with the layer in phase 4.",
